BUG: Terminal Persistence Fails (Mixed JS/Python State Logic + REST Overhead)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

SYMPTOMS:
  - Terminal creates new shell every time user leaves and returns to app
  - Terminal history lost on page reload
  - Multiple orphaned terminal shells pile up
  - Excessive REST endpoint calls (shell-id GET/POST, create, resize)
  - 500 errors on /terminal/auto/resize endpoint
  - JavaScript managing shell lifecycle instead of backend

ROOT CAUSE:
  1. Frontend had complex shell validation/cleanup logic in JavaScript
  2. Backend HistoryStore was being created fresh on each request (no singleton)
  3. Terminal ID stored in file but Python couldn't read it (new instance every time)
  4. Frontend calling REST endpoints with 'auto' before real shell ID arrived
  5. Architecture had unnecessary REST layer between frontend and WebSocket

CONVERSATION SUMMARY:
  1. User reported terminal not persisting across page reloads
  2. Agent discovered frontend doing shell validation/cleanup (should be backend)
  3. Added backend singleton for HistoryStore to persist state across requests
  4. User questioned why REST endpoints exist at all for terminal
  5. Agent realized correct architecture: WebSocket should handle everything
  6. Removed all frontend shell management logic
  7. Moved shell validation, orphan cleanup, and persistence to WebSocket handler
  8. Frontend now just connects to /ws/terminal/auto
  9. Backend sends real shell_id via WebSocket JSON message
  10. User caught resize errors - frontend using 'auto' before ID received
  11. Agent fixed timing: shellId stays null until WebSocket sends real ID
  12. User caught bug: create_editor_shell() signature doesn't accept mgr parameter
  13. Fixed function call signature
  14. Terminal now works with zero REST calls!

FILES MODIFIED:
  - app/apps/file_editor_cm6/terminal_backend.py
      * Added _history_store_singleton module-level variable
      * Added get_history_store() singleton factory function
      * Updated GET /terminal/shell-id to use singleton (endpoint kept for log fetching)
      * Updated POST /terminal/shell-id to use singleton
      * Enhanced WebSocket handler to accept shell_id='auto'
      * Added auto shell management in WebSocket:
        - Loads saved shell ID from history store
        - Cleans up orphaned terminal shells (except saved one)
        - Validates saved shell still exists and is running
        - Creates new shell if none exists or saved is dead
        - Saves new shell ID to history store
        - Sends shell_id to client via JSON message
      * Added detailed logging at each step for debugging
      * Fixed create_editor_shell() call to use cwd= keyword arg only
  
  - app/apps/file_editor_cm6/static/js/terminal.js
      * Removed all shell management logic from getOrCreateShell()
      * Changed to return null (no longer manages shell ID)
      * Updated open() to always connect to /ws/terminal/auto
      * Updated WebSocket onmessage handler to parse JSON messages:
        - Handles {"type": "shell_id", "shell_id": "..."} 
        - Updates shellId variable when received
        - Fetches log history after ID received
        - Handles {"type": "error", "message": "..."}
        - Treats non-JSON as terminal output
      * Removed orphan cleanup logic (cleanupOrphanedShells function)
      * shellId stays null until WebSocket provides real ID
      * Resize calls have if(shellId) guard - only fire after ID received
  
  - app/extensions/apps/main.py
      * Added Cache-Control headers to JS/CSS file serving
      * Forces browser to fetch fresh code on every load
      * Prevents stale JavaScript cache issues

ARCHITECTURE BEFORE:
```
Frontend → GET /terminal/shell-id → Returns saved ID or null
Frontend → Validates shell exists via GET /terminal/{id}
Frontend → Cleans up orphans via DELETE /terminal/{id}
Frontend → POST /terminal/create → Creates new shell
Frontend → POST /terminal/shell-id → Saves new ID
Frontend → WS /ws/terminal/{id} → Connects to PTY
Frontend → POST /terminal/{id}/resize → On every resize
```

ARCHITECTURE AFTER:
```
Frontend → WS /ws/terminal/auto → Backend handles everything
Backend  → Validates/cleans/creates/persists shell
Backend  → {"type": "shell_id", "shell_id": "fs_..."} → Frontend
Frontend → Uses real ID for subsequent calls (logs, resize)
```

FIX APPLIED:
  ✓ Terminal persistence moved entirely to backend
  ✓ HistoryStore made singleton to persist across requests
  ✓ WebSocket handler manages shell lifecycle
  ✓ Frontend simplified to just connect and receive ID
  ✓ Zero REST calls for shell management
  ✓ Terminal persists across page reloads
  ✓ Orphan cleanup happens automatically on reconnect
  ✓ Shell history restored via log tail fetch

VERIFICATION:
  - Terminal opens → Backend creates shell → SUCCESS
  - User leaves app → Shell stays alive → SUCCESS
  - User returns → Backend reconnects to same shell → SUCCESS
  - Terminal history shows previous session → SUCCESS
  - Only 1 shell exists (orphans cleaned) → SUCCESS
  - WebSocket logs show:
      [Terminal WS] Auto shell management requested
      [Terminal WS] Saved shell ID from history: fs_1762398196_de03c5c9
      [Terminal WS] Found 0 orphaned terminal shells
      [Terminal WS] Reconnecting to existing shell: fs_1762398196_de03c5c9
      [Terminal WS] Sending shell_id to client: fs_1762398196_de03c5c9

